Notebook[{Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Circular Lining Calculation Workbook", 
      "Title", ExpressionUUID -> "1df1fb83-272e-4b52-85d6-40e4376b6a35"], 
     Cell["Corrugated steel, plain concrete, and reinforced concrete", 
      "Subtitle", ExpressionUUID -> "17758d7a-8a64-4033-a4a9-003b13496cc1"], 
     Cell["R is the calculation engine. This workbook defines one engineering \
input set, evaluates it once, and presents the returned results for three \
independent lining solutions.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
       "4d228384-5caf-4110-ad4c-7167d67cdb5a"], 
     Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["1. Read first", "Chapter", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "c359f8db-96ec-d4f3-d173-9b5d63bcf522"], 
        Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["1.1 How to use this workbook", "Section", 
            ExpressionUUID -> "0d5684a1-9d57-627b-6d9e-05297f8779c4"], 
           Cell["1. Start with a fresh Wolfram kernel.\n2. Edit only the six \
pale-yellow engineering-input cells. They use the same field names as \
calculation.json. Editing the notebook recalculates the workbook but does not \
rewrite calculation.json; to regenerate the HTML report, copy the accepted \
values to calculation.json and run the report workflow.\n3. Section 2.1 \
controls cover. Section 2.2 / GroundInputs controls unit weight, surcharge, \
ground stiffness, the K0 model, friction angle, OCR, and net water pressure; \
K0 is derived and is not typed as a constant. Section 2.3 / SteelInputs \
controls the corrugated profile, remaining base thickness \
(remainingBaseThicknessMm), radius, and steel strengths. Section 2.5 / \
PlainConcreteInputs controls plain-shotcrete thickness (thicknessM) and \
concrete strength (compressiveStrengthMPa). Section 2.6 / \
ReinforcedConcreteInputs controls reinforced-shotcrete thickness and concrete \
strength, reinforcement grade, bar diameter, spacing, clear-cover ratio, and \
steel modulus. R derives bar area, reinforcement per face and direction, \
layer coordinates, reinforcement ratio, and every P-M domain; do not type a \
derived steel area directly.\n4. The 34 input leaves comprise 31 editable \
primitive values or conditions and three catalog-reference selections. \
Calculation-method constants are read-only and are returned with the results.\
\n5. For a first run, evaluate the complete notebook from a fresh kernel. The \
workbook loads the setup once and calls R once.\n6. After changing inputs, \
reevaluate the edited input cell, Section 3.2 (EngineeringInputs), Section 3.3 \
(Evaluate once), and the affected result section. The configured P-M curve \
and checks will update; the discrete curves, beginning with the historical \
minimum, remain visible for comparison.\n7. Review the normalized inputs, \
derived mesh, three solution sections, nine circular diagrams, and the P-M \
interaction family before adopting a design.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
             "113fef14-4500-d119-28ac-c1c0411dae88"]}, Open]], 
        Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["1.2 Input-to-result map", "Section", 
            ExpressionUUID -> "80a04672-ce4c-d972-287a-8aec48d8222a"], 
           Cell["Cover geometry \[LongDash] fill height and the independent \
crown-to-axis distance.\nFill and ground state \[LongDash] effective fill \
action, ground stiffness, friction angle, OCR, net water pressure, and the \
derived K0.\nCorrugated-steel lining \[LongDash] \
catalog section, independent steel radius, remaining thickness, and material \
properties.\nSeam and corrosion \[LongDash] published reference selection, \
initial diameter, and relative diameter loss.\nPlain-concrete lining \
\[LongDash] independent outer radius, thickness, material, and construction \
condition.\nReinforced-concrete lining and reinforcement \[LongDash] \
independent outer radius, thickness, concrete material, reinforcement grade, \
bar diameter, spacing, clear-cover ratio, and reinforcement modulus; R \
derives bar area, layer coordinates, steel area, and yield strength.\nThe crown-to-axis distance, steel centroidal \
radius, plain-concrete outer radius, and reinforced-concrete outer radius are \
four separate inputs even when their defaults are equal.", "Text", 
            ExpressionUUID -> "47e1ac61-872d-1664-76ea-4e3cd26838f3"]}, 
          Open]]}, Open]], Cell[CellGroupData[
       {Cell["2. Engineering inputs", "Chapter", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "b4b8dfd2-6f36-b56a-6444-5fb45b0bd091"], Cell["Edit the project \
values in these six groups. Calculation-method constants are read-only and \
are presented with the resolved results.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "d3fd45cf-2f41-b35b-8e4e-a1ff4823dbfb"], 
        Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["2.1 Cover geometry", "Section", 
            ExpressionUUID -> "5f96bf15-fc82-44bb-b4cc-5c36af3be913"], 
